## Find the angle PSH
$P$ is the incentre, so $[SP]$ bisects $\angle HSG$.
|\angle PSH| &= \frac{30.75}{2}
&= 15.375^\circ
## Find |PS| using the right-angled triangle at the tangent point
The radius $11.3$ is perpendicular to $[SH]$, so it is opposite $\angle PSH$, and $|PS|$ is the hypotenuse.
\sin 15.375^\circ &= \frac{11.3}{|PS|}
|PS| &= \frac{11.3}{\sin 15.375^\circ}
&= 42.62
## Use the angle of elevation to find the pole height
$[ST]$ is vertical and $|PS|$ is horizontal, so the angle at $P$ is in a right-angled triangle $PST$.
\tan 14^\circ &= \frac{|ST|}{|PS|}
|ST| &= 42.62 \tan 14^\circ
&= 10.626
&\approx 10.6 \text{ m}
ANSWER: 10.6 \text{ m}

## Convert metres per second to metres per hour
There are $60$ seconds in a minute and $60$ minutes in an hour.
1.6 \times 60 &= 96 \text{ metres per minute}
96 \times 60 &= 5760 \text{ metres per hour}
## Convert metres to kilometres
There are $1000$ metres in a kilometre, so divide by $1000$.
5760 \div 1000 &= 5.76
ANSWER: 5.76 \text{ km/h}

## Substitute R = 2500 and T = 480
P &= \frac{480 \times 2500}{5252}
&= \frac{1200000}{5252}
## Calculate and round
&\approx 228.48
&\approx 228
ANSWER: P = 228 \text{ horsepower}

## Multiply both sides by 5252
P &= \frac{R \times T}{5252}
5252P &= R \times T
## Divide both sides by T
R &= \frac{5252P}{T}
ANSWER: R = \frac{5252P}{T}
